IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-companies-domain`

§ `Part 12 — General`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 12, ss 386A–411.
-- Source: SSO current version as at 07 Sep 2026.
--
-- Division 1: Enforcement (service, electronic communications, records)
-- Division 2: Offences (false statements, fraud, dividends, penalties)
-- Division 3: Miscellaneous (appeals, composition, regulations)
--
-- This encoding covers the computable thresholds and penalties.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `Division 1 — Enforcement`


§§§ `s 390 — Disposal of shares of missing shareholder`

-- s 390(1): shareholder whereabouts unknown >= 10 years
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 390(1)"
`missing shareholder years before disposal` MEANS 10

-- s 390(1): 1 month after advertisement before transfer
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 390(1)"
`missing shareholder advertisement months` MEANS 1


§§§ `s 396B — Liability for improper accounts`

-- s 396B(1)(a): 2-year lookback period
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 396B(1)(a)"
`improper accounts lookback years` MEANS 2

-- s 396B(1): penalty
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 396B(1)"
`penalty for improper accounts` MEANS 5000
`imprisonment for improper accounts months` MEANS 12


§§§ `s 397 — Translations`

-- s 397(3): translate records at intervals of not more than 7 days
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 397(3)"
`record translation interval days` MEANS 7


§§ `Division 2 — Offences`


§§§ `s 401 — False and misleading statements`

-- s 401(2): penalty for false/misleading statements in required documents
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 401(2)"
`penalty for false statement in document` MEANS 50000
`imprisonment for false statement years` MEANS 2


§§§ `s 402 — False reports to officers`

-- s 402(1): penalty
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 402(1)"
`penalty for false report to officer` MEANS 10000
`imprisonment for false report years` MEANS 2


§§§ `s 403 — Dividends from profits only`

-- s 403(2): penalty for paying dividends not from profits
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 403(2)"
`penalty for improper dividend` MEANS 5000
`imprisonment for improper dividend months` MEANS 12


§§§ `s 404 — Fraudulently inducing investment`

-- s 404(3): penalty for obtaining money by false promise
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 404(3)"
`penalty for fraudulent inducement` MEANS 15000
`imprisonment for fraudulent inducement years` MEANS 5


§§§ `s 406 — Frauds by officers`

-- s 406: general officer fraud — 2-month lookback for property concealment
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 406(c)"
`officer fraud property concealment lookback months` MEANS 2

-- s 406: penalty
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 406"
`penalty for officer fraud` MEANS 15000
`imprisonment for officer fraud years` MEANS 3


§§§ `s 407 — General penalty`

-- s 407(2): default penalty where none specified
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 407(2)"
`default penalty for unspecified offence` MEANS 1000


§§§ `s 408 — Default penalties`

-- s 408(1): daily default penalty where not specified
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 408(1)"
`default daily penalty` MEANS 200


§§ `Division 3 — Miscellaneous`


§§§ `s 409B — Composition of offences`

-- s 409B(1): composition cap — half of max fine or $20,000, whichever lower
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 409B(1)"
`composition maximum` MEANS 20000

GIVEN `maximum fine for offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `composition amount cap` IS
    IF (`maximum fine for offence` DIVIDED BY 2) AT MOST 20000
    THEN `maximum fine for offence` DIVIDED BY 2
    ELSE 20000


§§§ `s 409C — Appeal to Court`

-- s 409C(1): 28 days to appeal Registrar's decision
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 409C(1)"
`registrar decision appeal days` MEANS 28


-- ===========================================================================
-- TEST CASES
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Part 12 — Illustrations`

-- s 409B: composition amount cap
-- Max fine $10,000 -> half = $5,000 < $20,000 -> cap is $5,000
#ASSERT (`composition amount cap` 10000) EQUALS 5000
-- Max fine $50,000 -> half = $25,000 > $20,000 -> cap is $20,000
#ASSERT (`composition amount cap` 50000) EQUALS 20000
-- Max fine $40,000 -> half = $20,000 = $20,000 -> cap is $20,000
#ASSERT (`composition amount cap` 40000) EQUALS 20000

-- Constant assertions
#ASSERT `missing shareholder years before disposal` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `default penalty for unspecified offence` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `default daily penalty` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `registrar decision appeal days` EQUALS 28
